\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Comparing fields carried to one vertex}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Take the two-component fields in \ref{fdip-00WV},
now at different vertices. A path from either vertex
to a common destination gives a
[represented transport](fdip-00WD) for that field.
After transport, both fields have components in the
same fiber. How can a fixed multilinear contraction
of these components respect all endpoint changes of
basis while retaining the order of the odd factors?}
